SUMMARY:The KV Cache Bottleneck: Architectural Alternatives
DESCRIPTION:Get up-to-date information at: https://luma.com/587afpgo\n\nAdd
 ress:\nCheck event page for more details.\n\nIn autoregressive decoding, e
 ach new token recomputes the keys and values for all preceding tokens. Thi
 s cache grows linearly with context length, and in long-context serving it
  becomes the dominant memory and bandwidth cost - quite often more limitin
 g than raw compute itself.\nIn this session, Host 27 Quill, co-founder of 
 FrontiersMind, shall walk through the main architectural responses to this
  problem and what each one costs us. Grouped-query and multi-query attenti
 on bring down the number of KV heads. Cross-layer sharing Cross-Layer Atte
 ntion and the shared KV cache in the recent Gemma…\n\nHosted by Team Los
 sfunk, Host 2 Quill & Host 3 Quill
LOCATION:https://luma.com/event/evt-8Mu36DRxrQV4ttX
GEO:12.980070469169066;77.64139348744976
SEQUENCE:214291074
STATUS:TENTATIVE
END:VEVENT
